In article <stevegC88J3G.H8x@netcom.com> steveg@netcom.com (Steve Garritano) writes:
> 1) How do you eat food when fainting without fainting over and over again?
>    Once you start fainting from lack of food, all I can do is pray to
>    my deity for food.

I consider this a bug.  It should be fixed, and perhaps will be in
3.1.2.  Meanwhile, lembas wafers have high nutritional value, and not
much weight.  Perhaps they will help (or perhaps not...I never let
my character get so hungry if he has something to eat!).

> 2) In version 3.0, you usually vomit if you eat too much, but now, you
>    ALWAYS choke over your food. That eliminates the easiest way to rid
>    a disease from tainted meat. :-0   How do you cure diseases?

Use a spell or a unicorn horn.  I believe extra healing will help, as
well.

> 3) How do you protect yourself from touches of death?

Magic resistance.  Get it via gray dragon scale mail, cloak of magic
resistance, wielding Magicbane, or simply holding some of the quest
artifacts.

> 4) Is there _any_ trap that _anyone_ can untrap? (What a waste of key!)

The ones on doors and chests can be untrapped if you have high enough
dexterity.  Supposedly.  It's never worked for me.

> 5) How do you find traps on booby-trapped doors and chests?

Use the #untrap command, of course.

> About genociding gelatinous cubes (very minor possible spoiler).
> Why would anyone genocide gelatinous cubes? Eating them can give you cold
> resistance, fire resistance, shock resistance, and possibly more. They
> are *very* easy to destroy by the time you encounter them.

This was more common in 3.0.  They could paralyze you for quite
awhile.  Still, they have this annoying tendency to eat anything left
laying around, especially wood and leather.

